WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:08.560
KlimateX turns a Lagos family's switch from a petrol generator to solar into verified carbon credits, and pays the family their share.

00:00:09.060 --> 00:00:13.780
It is one platform, with a dashboard for everyone in the chain. Here they are.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:25.470
Families use the phone app. Adaeze signs in with her phone number and a PIN. She sees her grade, the petrol she saved, and what she has been paid, straight into her Access Bank solar loan.

00:00:25.970 --> 00:00:38.290
The app tells her how to earn more, from her own readings: add last year's fuel receipts, and run the backup generator less. She can ask questions by typing or by voice, in five languages.

00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:43.940
Every figure can be checked: the working for each month, and a home energy certificate.

00:00:44.440 --> 00:00:46.880
The same household dashboard runs on the web.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:51.320
Installers see every home they fitted, and which ones need attention.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:59.220
Auditors review the evidence, sample homes, and sign off each period. Nine checks run on every home's readings.

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:05.310
Companies buy and retire the credits in the marketplace. Half of every sale goes to the family.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:09.090
Access Bank sees its solar loans by measured energy grade.

00:01:09.590 --> 00:01:13.880
Our operations team sees every home, payout and loan in one view.

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:19.190
And anyone can see how clean their street's power is, or check a credit's serial.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.410
KlimateX. Measured, audited, and paid.

